  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does a kitchen remodel cost in Orlando?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Kitchen remodeling investment depends on scope \u2014 a refresh that keeps your layout is a very different project from a full custom kitchen that moves walls, reworks plumbing and electrical, and installs custom cabinetry and stone. KBF begins by establishing a target investment together, then aligns the design, selections, and construction scope to that target. After the in-home consultation and design development, you receive a fixed-scope written estimate before work begins. Any later change is documented and approved in writing before it affects cost or schedule."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does a kitchen remodel take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A typical KBF kitchen remodel takes 6 to 10 weeks from demolition to final walkthrough, with design and permitting adding another 4 to 6 weeks before construction starts. Cabinet lead times, layout changes that touch plumbing or electrical, and Orange County inspection scheduling are the most common variables. We give you a written project schedule at contract signing and update it weekly."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need a permit to remodel my kitchen in Florida?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Any kitchen remodel that involves moving plumbing, electrical, gas, or load-bearing walls requires a permit from the local building department (Orange County, City of Orlando, or your municipality). Cosmetic updates like cabinet refacing, countertop replacement, or paint typically do not. KBF pulls all required permits as part of the project and handles inspections directly, so you don't navigate the county portal."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between a kitchen refacing and a full custom remodel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Refacing keeps your existing cabinet boxes and replaces only the doors, drawer fronts, and hardware \u2014 a faster, lighter project that is typically completed in 1\u20132 weeks. A full custom remodel replaces cabinets, countertops, appliances, flooring, and lighting, and often reconfigures the layout \u2014 a larger project that is usually completed in 6\u201310 weeks. Refacing makes sense when your layout works and your boxes are solid; a remodel makes sense when the layout fights you or the kitchen is dated end-to-end."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I stay in my home during a kitchen remodel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most KBF clients stay in their home during the remodel. Your kitchen will be unusable for 3 to 6 weeks during the construction phase, so we help you set up a temporary kitchen space (microwave, mini-fridge, prep area) before demolition starts. Dust containment, daily cleanup, and protected pathways through the work zone are standard on every KBF project."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's included in a KBF custom kitchen design?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "KBF custom kitchens include layout design, 3D renderings, cabinet selection and installation, countertops, backsplash, flooring, lighting, plumbing fixtures, and appliance coordination \u2014 managed by one project team from concept to final walkthrough. You get one point of contact, one schedule, and one warranty, instead of coordinating a designer, a GC, and a cabinet vendor separately."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What kitchen styles work best for Orlando homes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Transitional and modern-coastal styles dominate Orlando kitchens right now \u2014 clean Shaker or slab cabinetry in white, warm wood, or soft gray; quartz or quartzite countertops; oversized islands; and large-format porcelain or LVP flooring that holds up to Florida humidity. We also see strong demand for outdoor-kitchen tie-ins on lanai and pool-deck builds, given the year-round Central Florida climate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does KBF handle cabinets, countertops, and appliances, or do I source those?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "KBF sources and installs everything \u2014 cabinets, countertops, hardware, tile, fixtures, and (optionally) appliances. We work with a curated set of premium cabinet manufacturers and stone fabricators, and pass our trade pricing through to you. If you've already purchased an appliance package or want to bring your own slab, we can absolutely work it in."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you handle changes mid-project?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Every change is documented in a written change order with a fixed price and a schedule impact before any work is done \u2014 no surprise line items at the end. Most KBF projects have 1 to 3 small change orders (an extra outlet, a different tile, a hardware swap) and they're priced and signed in 24 to 48 hours."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I get started with a KBF kitchen remodel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Start with a free in-home consultation \u2014 we walk your space, talk through goals and budget, and within 5 to 7 business days you'll have a written ballpark estimate. Once you sign the design agreement, we produce 3D renderings, finalize selections, and issue a fixed-scope construction contract before any demolition."
      }
    }
  ]
}

